1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:03,048
Now, Bun's WebSocket feature does also have

2
00:00:03,176 --> 00:00:06,048
a client version. It's not in the browser,

3
00:00:06,128 --> 00:00:08,807
there we use the browser API, but you could

4
00:00:08,936 --> 00:00:12,257
build a CLI WebSocket client, for example,

5
00:00:12,385 --> 00:00:14,439
or some other client that's powered by Bun.

6
00:00:15,193 --> 00:00:18,016
So here in the CLI client.ts file, I have a

7
00:00:18,016 --> 00:00:20,439
very simple CLI where I get some

8
00:00:21,209 --> 00:00:24,658
input from the user for the username and the

9
00:00:24,723 --> 00:00:27,049
room, or I assume some defaults if no

10
00:00:27,129 --> 00:00:29,327
arguments were passed to the CLI command.

11
00:00:30,674 --> 00:00:32,551
And then just as in the browser, we

12
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:35,357
establish a connection by preparing a URL

13
00:00:35,887 --> 00:00:38,902
and using that same WebSocket API we used in

14
00:00:38,934 --> 00:00:39,415
the browser.

15
00:00:39,976 --> 00:00:42,462
But this file will not be executed by the

16
00:00:42,462 --> 00:00:45,349
browser. It will be executed by Bun because

17
00:00:45,349 --> 00:00:48,396
in my package.json file, it's this CLI

18
00:00:48,396 --> 00:00:51,011
script that would execute that file using

19
00:00:51,123 --> 00:00:52,165
Bun as you see.

20
00:00:53,208 --> 00:00:55,806
But Bun, just like the browser, also

21
00:00:55,854 --> 00:00:58,500
supports this WebSocket API, the standard

22
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:58,805
web WebSocket API.

23
00:00:59,945 --> 00:01:02,530
Just as Bun supports the standard response

24
00:01:02,594 --> 00:01:04,377
or request APIs, for example.

25
00:01:05,083 --> 00:01:07,154
And therefore we can use WebSockets here

26
00:01:07,154 --> 00:01:09,290
just as we did in the browser, listen to the

27
00:01:09,338 --> 00:01:11,907
same kind of events, use the same API

28
00:01:11,987 --> 00:01:14,091
because it is the same API

29
00:01:14,637 --> 00:01:15,970
but now powered by Bun.

30
00:01:16,564 --> 00:01:18,458
So with the Bun server still up and running,

31
00:01:18,956 --> 00:01:20,530
I could run bun run CLI

32
00:01:21,445 --> 00:01:24,094
and maybe connect as Max to chat.

33
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:26,776
So now Max joined chat

34
00:01:27,322 --> 00:01:28,397
and I could say, hi there,

35
00:01:29,409 --> 00:01:31,095
and see my message here and then open

36
00:01:31,095 --> 00:01:32,492
another CLI session.

37
00:01:33,279 --> 00:01:34,499
So run bun run CLI

38
00:01:35,976 --> 00:01:39,123
Andy and same topic, same room chat.

39
00:01:40,488 --> 00:01:41,339
Hi, this is

40
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:46,124
Andy. And if I do that, you'll see in the

41
00:01:46,124 --> 00:01:46,846
Max chat,

42
00:01:47,376 --> 00:01:48,966
I see, hi, this is Andy.

43
00:01:50,202 --> 00:01:50,781
And if I write

44
00:01:51,328 --> 00:01:53,417
hi there, of course, as Max,

45
00:01:54,623 --> 00:01:57,451
that also shows up here. So same logic, but

46
00:01:57,516 --> 00:02:01,072
now this is a Bun client. This is not a web

47
00:02:01,234 --> 00:02:03,359
client. If I close my session here with

48
00:02:03,489 --> 00:02:05,045
Andy, I also see that message here.

49
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:09,605
And therefore you can use Bun not just for

50
00:02:09,605 --> 00:02:12,453
setting up a server, but also for setting up

51
00:02:12,453 --> 00:02:13,836
a client if you want to.
